NOTE ON THE VAT-GUARD GATE (found in this round, not reported by the reviewer)
  Round 5 added a `vatType` write to `expenseClaimService.postClaimToGl`, which
  put that file in scope for scripts/ci/check-vat-guard-coverage.ts and FAILED
  the gate at 47e73f95b — i.e. `bun run ci` was red on the branch as scored.
  Disposed as an ATTENDED allowlist entry with the argument the gate asks for:
  `postClaimToGl` has one caller (`expense-claims/[id]/post`, a person clicking
  Post to GL on one claim), the approve endpoint hands back
  INPUT_VAT_DENIED_ADVICE and the detail page now renders it, and the file picks
  no account, holds no rate, and only LABELS a zero-VAT leg `no_vat`. Widening
  the guard-module regex to admit `claimVatAdvice` was rejected: it would let any
  future file count as guarded by importing a labeller.

